-- forge_nb.march — Notebook package management
--
-- Provides Forge.add() for use inside notebook cells.
-- Emits a sentinel line that the notebook server intercepts to run `forge add`.

mod Forge do

  doc """
  Add a dependency to the notebook's forge.toml, from inside a notebook cell.
  [spec] is passed verbatim to `forge add`. This prints the sentinel line
  `__FORGE_ADD__:<spec>` to stdout; the notebook server intercepts it, runs
  `forge add` in the notebook's directory and shows a toast once the
  dependency is installed, so later cells can use the package. Outside a
  notebook server it only prints that line.

  ## Examples

      Forge.add("json --git https://github.com/march-lang/json")
      Forge.add("utils --path ../my-utils")
      Forge.add("mylib --git https://github.com/me/mylib --tag v1.0")
  """
  fn add(spec) do
    println("__FORGE_ADD__:" ++ spec)
  end

end
